 "title": "Two readings of layers: a three-edge cut carries contradictions up, a parity name carries correlations",
 "subject": "How one level of a learned knot network can speak to the next",
 "conclusion": "Through a three-edge cut a lower level's unsatisfiable class becomes the upper level's constraint, so a dissonance crosses levels; through a parity name it cannot, and each level keeps its own (proved by hand). Names instead carry class-dependent correlations of the lower level's states, single clauses included, which no cut can offer (computed).",
